# spark in w3m -- your own AI, on your own machine (spark.forgewright.ai).
# Append these lines to your own ~/.w3m/keymap:
#
#     cat ~/.w3m/spark/keymap.spark >> ~/.w3m/keymap
#
#   M-s  the page you are reading goes to `spark read`: what does this
#        page cover? The answer opens in a new buffer, every line
#        quoting the page; B goes back.
#   M-a  w3m's pipe prompt, for a question: type `spark-w3m your words`
#        and press Enter. A page past 16 kB answers with its part count;
#        `spark-w3m --part 2 your words` reads part 2.
#
# spark-w3m is this repository's one-line wrapper around `spark read`:
# it folds spark's stderr into the answer, so a refusal ("the source
# does not answer -- it opens: ...") shows in the buffer instead of
# vanishing. Nothing leaves this machine but the rendered page text and
# your words, to the brain spark is configured for -- never the URL.
# Needs w3m 0.5.3 or newer and spark 1.20 or newer. M-s and M-a are
# suggestions -- edit the two lines to taste.
keymap M-s PIPE_BUF "spark-w3m"
keymap M-a PIPE_BUF
